{"4224460": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "SCP-3008: Infinite Store", "steam_appid": 4224460, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "detailed_description": "<span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4224460/extras/77ed1861f1bcd8f82757d50e328d180a.poster.avif?t=1773856810\" width=1170 height=658 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4224460/extras/77ed1861f1bcd8f82757d50e328d180a.webm?t=1773856810\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4224460/extras/77ed1861f1bcd8f82757d50e328d180a.mp4?t=1773856810\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >The Store looks familiar.</h2>That’s the problem.<br>You enter a brightly lit furniture superstore made of showrooms, aisles, and corridors.<br>Everything is clean. Orderly. Normal.<br>Then it repeats.<br>The rooms return in the same order, with the same layout — but not always in the same state. Something may be wrong. Or nothing may be wrong at all. And knowing the difference is the only way forward.<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4224460/extras/d3b5aeddfd5d7b4bd3061a78d3477dd0.poster.avif?t=1773856810\" width=1170 height=658 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4224460/extras/d3b5aeddfd5d7b4bd3061a78d3477dd0.webm?t=1773856810\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4224460/extras/d3b5aeddfd5d7b4bd3061a78d3477dd0.mp4?t=1773856810\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Observation is the game</h2>Each room you enter may contain an anomaly - or may be perfectly normal. If you notice something out of the ordinary, turn back. If everything appears normal, move forward. Choose incorrectly, and the loop resets. <br>There is no combat, no hints, and no confirmation. The Store never tells you what changed - only if you were right or wrong.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Your objective</h2>You are not just trying to escape - you are shopping! As you move through the Store, you must collect items from a shopping list scattered naturally throughout the rooms. Miss an item, and the Store will not let you leave.<br>Every reset reshuffles your list and your path. Routine turns into pressure the longer each loop continues.<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4224460/extras/8f40c90d4d1614be4859a9381aa6c59b.poster.avif?t=1773856810\" width=1170 height=658 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4224460/extras/8f40c90d4d1614be4859a9381aa6c59b.webm?t=1773856810\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4224460/extras/8f40c90d4d1614be4859a9381aa6c59b.mp4?t=1773856810\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >The end of the loop</h2>Reach the cash-out room with all required items, and the Store may finally allow you to leave.<br>Or it may not.<br><br>Every playthrough begins again in the first room.<br>Nothing is permanent except what you remember.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Key Features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>Observation-Driven Progression</strong><br> Advance by noticing what feels wrong — or realizing nothing is.<br></li><li><strong>Endless Marketplace Loop</strong><br> A furniture superstore layout built from themed rooms and corridors that repeat, reset, and deceive.<br></li><li><strong>Unique Anomalies</strong><br> Environmental, audio, and entity-based changes designed to test perception, not reflexes.<br></li><li